I've written the complete `DESIGN.md` to `/src/mxfs/DESIGN.md` as requested — a from-scratch reference covering: what MXFS is and why shared-LUN coherency is hard; the full on-disk envelope layout (4KB super → journal → disklock region with heartbeat+eviction-ring and the 65536×512B CAW slot table → XFS region); the DLM (lock modes, slot format, the CAW acquire/release algorithm, BAST via disk-poll-on-`waiters` with UDP as a mere hint, the per-inode in-core state machine, deferred publish, transport selection); the cache-coherency mechanisms (drain pipeline/invariant #1, FUA reads, dir-gen counters, publish-before-notify, inode-reuse eviction); invariants; fencing/recovery; build/test/tools; and a deep section on the remaining `cache_coherency` bug with the epoch-in-slot fix direction.

It also bakes in the correction from your catch: **the network is never correctness-bearing** — lock correctness is 100% disk (SCSI CAW + the disk-polled `waiters` bit); UDP multicast BAST is only a latency hint, and the "lossy" channel is the on-disk eviction *ring* (a ring-buffer overwrite), not packet loss.

